# Threat detection rules that set a transaction bit outside of an app-layer
# hook. Such a rule has no transaction of its own, so the set must be a no-op:
# it must not act on whatever transaction the thread inspected last.
# IP-only rule: runs on the first packet of each flow, before any app-layer.
alert tcp any any -> any any (xbits:set,txb1,track tx; sid:200; rev:1;)
# packet rule on established flows
alert tcp any any -> any any (flow:established; xbits:set,txb2,track tx; sid:201; rev:1;)
